'''Legend Quest''' (レジェンドクエスト, ''Rejendo Kuesuto'', '''Legend Quest''') is an event added in [[Version 8.6 Update|Version 8.6]]. It is available after clearing [[Empire of Cats]] Chapter 1.
{{Map Stars|4095}}

==Overview==
Legend Quest is a map somewhat similar to [[Heavenly Tower]], with 48 stages known as LEVELs. Each LEVEL is a random [[Stories of Legend]] stage that provides a partially randomized lineup. All LEVELs are [[No Continues]], and exiting a battle within 10 seconds will not refund [[Battle Items|items]], Crowns or [[Cat Energy|energy]].

==Play Requirements==
===Stage Clear Requirements===
To play LEVEL x, the player must first beat Stories of Legend sub-chapter x + 1. For example, in order to play LEVEL 4 of Legend Quest, the player will need to have beaten Stories of Legend sub-chapter 5, [[Risqué Terrain]]. From LEVEL 11 onward, there is an added requirement of having a [[User Rank]] of 1600 or more.

===Cost Requirements===
In addition to energy, the LEVELs require Crowns to access. The player will begin with a set amount of Crowns, which is equal to the number of Stories of Legend Crown difficulties they have cleared. Crowns obtained from [[Uncanny Legends]] or [[Zero Legends]] do not count here.
[[File:Sol1.png|thumb|right|60px|A Crown]]
The maximum number of Crowns that the player can have is 196. Crowns spent in Legend Quest do not impact the player's progress in Stories of Legend. Unlike Energy, they do not regenerate over time, but are instead fully restored with each reappearance of the event. Every time the player retries a LEVEL, the Crown cost increases by 1, maxing out at 4 Crowns for LEVELs 1~40 and 5 Crowns for LEVELs 41~48.

==Randomization==
===Stage Randomization===
Legend Quest's LEVELs are randomized. Upon starting LEVEL x, the game will pick a random stage from Stories of Legend sub-chapter x to x + 1. For example, LEVEL 1 is a random stage from [[The Legend Begins]] or [[Passion Land]]. However, it is not completely random, as LAST LEVEL (48) will always be [[Eldritch Forces]] from [[Laboratory of Relics]]. Once a stage is picked, it will not change until the event's next appearance. Stages are always on 1-Crown difficulty and all enemies that appear in them are visible even before attempting.

===Lineup Randomization===
Legend Quest will change the player's lineup upon entering a LEVEL as its main source of difficulty. Cats will be swapped with random other cats that the player has, potentially preventing the player from even passing a stage if they end up with an unsuitable formation, as many require a dedicated specialist lineup or at least a few key units. The number of cats swapped is generally random, though it will never replace all 10, nor will it change its current form (i.e., if [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cat]] is currently selected, its form will not be changed to Macho Cat or Mohawk Cat), and empty slots in a lineup will not be filled. The more the player attempts a LEVEL, the less likely it is for a Cat Unit to be swapped.

