==Recommendations==
*Complete as many Stories of Legend Crown difficulties as possible so more retries are available, as Crown consumption accumulates quickly if they cannot be cleared in one or two attempts. Once you get to around LEVEL 20, do not expect to beat the stages in one try without a proper formation.
*Upgrade every Cat Unit you have that could potentially be helpful, especially the ones with generalist traits. It would be distasteful to receive [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Figure Skating Cats]] but at a low level.
*Take time to study each stage and do some planning. Knowing the stage mechanics allows you to know how to beat the stages even with random cats. If it isn't obvious how to tackle a stage, you can try to identify it and look up the corresponding stage.
*Remember to pause and check each randomized unit's abilities through the "Confirm Units" button. Knowing what you have to work with is always important. It's a good idea to change your cats' forms before entering any stage, depending on their level. Because of this, you can easily tell which cats are worth putting on the battlefield, while others stay behind.
**In a similar vein, keeping a few of your [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]] in their Evolved Forms may be worth considering so you have a higher chance to get a meatshield.
*When possible, bring multiple good counters for an enemy/situation you foresee to be troublesome. For example, if the stage has [[Razorback]], bring many solid black stallers such as [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Bombercat]], [[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Wargod Nobunaga]] and [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Cat Eastwood]]. This way, if one of them gets swapped, you might still have others to keep you going.
*Consider investing in [[Talents]], so that units can serve more purposes if you roll them. For example, Cameraman Cat may appear useless on a metal stage at first, but her Critical talent could turn things around despite the 2% chance.
*Avoid units who are only useful in presence of specific others, such as those who exclusively help through [[Cat Combo]]s, or in a rush-down approach that needs another rusher, as that other rusher or combo constituent may be swapped away, removing two or more good units with one swap.
*If you are more concerned about items than Crowns, try stages a couple times before resorting to using them, as you are more likely to keep the necessary units for a stage if you already failed it a few times. If saving up Crowns is the higher priority, using items if needed and crossing your fingers is instead preferable.
*Even if you know a run is doomed based on the randomly selected cats, it's still important to play it out, to get a feel for enemy timing. Occasionally, you'll be surprised and find it isn't actually impossible.
*Have fun! No matter how skilled or how knowledgeable you are, Legend Quest is still all about luck. Try not get stressed out with the wrong cats that get picked for you. Just laugh it off and continue fighting until you burn out or get lucky enough to beat this entire challenge.

