==Trivia==
*Prior to [[Version 10.7 Update|Version 10.7]], Legend Quest used Stars instead of Crowns. Oddly, the tutorial shown when tapping the Crown icon wasn't updated to reflect this until much later.
*Legend Quest's logo is heavily based on ''[[wikipedia:Dragon Quest|Dragon Quest]]''<nowiki>'</nowiki>s.
*In [[Nyanko Daisensou|BCJP]], Legend Quest's logo in the event poster has a very different subtitle from the [[The Battle Cats|English Version]]'s: 天空の大地と過ぎ去りし伝説の物語 (''Tenkū no Daichi to Sugisarishi Densetsu no Monogatari'', "Heavenly Land and a Passing Story of Legend"). Everything before 伝説の物語 ("Story of Legend") is a mash-up of three of the ''Dragon Quest'' games' Japanese subtitles:
**天空の (''Tenkū no'', "Heavenly") is from [https://dragon-quest.org/wiki/Dragon_Quest_V:_Hand_of_the_Heavenly_Bride ''Dragon Quest V'']'s Japanese subtitle, 天空の花嫁 (''Tenkū no Hanayome'', "Heavenly Bride")
**大地 (''Daichi'', "Land") is from [https://dragon-quest.org/wiki/Dragon_Quest_VI:_Realms_of_Revelation ''Dragon Quest VI'']'s Japanese subtitle, 幻の大地 (''Maboroshi no Daichi'', "Land of Illusion")
**過ぎ去りし (''Sugisarashi'', "Passing") is from [https://dragon-quest.org/wiki/Dragon_Quest_XI:_Echoes_of_an_Elusive_Age ''Dragon Quest XI'']'s Japanese subtitle, 過ぎ去りし時を求めて (''Sugisarishi Toki o Motomete'', "In Search of a Passing Time").

